s, and first-term incumbent Jeff Hurd enters the fall with a clear financial edge, having raised $3.5 million and holding $1.8 million on hand to Democrat Dwayne Romero's $84,000. Expert raters split between Lean Republican and Likely Republican, with none calling the seat safe, and prediction markets give Romero roughly a three-in-ten chance.\n\nThe race is nonetheless competitive. The only published head-to-head poll, from July, showed Hurd ahead by a single point, and national Democrats have invested: the DCCC placed the district on its target list and named Romero to its Red to Blue program. A favorable national environment for Democrats keeps the seat within reach, but Hurd's incumbency, money and the district's underlying lean make him a modest favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2665, "margin": -3.72}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2864, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.288, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3508, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2424, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2636, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3101, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3157, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3103, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3134, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3018, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3083, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3049, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2686, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2627, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2161, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.264, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2504, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2452, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.323, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13